GUIDING PRINCIPLES OF SOA

1. Standardized Service Contract
2. Loose Coupling
3. Abstraction
4. Reusability
5. Composability
6. Discoverability
Meaning in simple language:
• Standardized Service Contract → Services follow a defined interface.
• Loose Coupling → Services have minimal dependency on each other.
• Abstraction → Internal implementation is hidden from the user.
• Reusability → Same service can be reused by different applications.
• Composability → Multiple services can be combined to create a larger application.
• Discoverability → Services can be easily found. 

